   {
    "chapter": "Week 1",
    "text": "Every living thing is built from cells, and every cell runs the same basic plan: a membrane-wrapped interior where organelles divide the work. The nucleus stores the DNA \u2014 the instruction set \u2014 while ribosomes build proteins from those instructions. Mitochondria release energy from food molecules, the cytoskeleton gives the cell its shape and moves materials around, and the cytoplasm is the gel where most chemistry happens. Plant cells add a rigid wall and chloroplasts; animal cells do without both. Structure is not decoration \u2014 each part exists because it does a job the whole cell depends on.",
